# Force LF on all shell/text assets, independent of the checkout platform.
#
# Why this matters: with Git's Windows default core.autocrlf=true, a clone would
# rewrite these files to CRLF on checkout. That breaks loop-kit two ways:
#   1. a CRLF shebang ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r") is a "bad interpreter" — loop.sh
#      and evaluate.sh won't start under Git Bash.
#   2. loop.config.sh is *sourced*, so every value would gain a trailing \r
#      (PERMISSION_MODE="acceptEdits"\r), corrupting the harness's own parsing.
# Pinning eol=lf keeps the Git Bash path (which the README endorses) working.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
